qcom-pon / qcom_battmgr / msm-poweroff / pmic-glink / ucsi-glink changes,
from the squashed liuqin downstream patch.

Adjustments for v7.2.5:
- drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c: v7.2.5 upstream reads the cell
  length and writes buf_len bytes with le32 handling equivalent to the
  downstream fix, but lacks the cell_bytes member and the cell-width
  sanity check; only that member and the probe-time width check are
  kept. A duplicated block from the squashed patch was dropped.
- drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c: a duplicated block from the
  squashed patch (XM structs/enums, raw members, xm request helpers,
  raw attribute group) was dropped.
- drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c: v7.2.5 has a different variant
  enum (SC8280XP/SM8350/SM8550/X1E80100); re-added QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8475
  and the qcom,sm8475-pmic-glink match entry at their new positions.
  The NOTIF_XM_PROPERTY define was dropped - v7.2.5 already has
  BATTMGR_XM_PROPERTY_GET/SET 0x50/0x51 and all SM8475 handling.

